{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_5>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Main instance = new Main();\n        instance.runProgram();\n    }\n\n    private void runProgram() {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = scanner.nextInt();\n        int k = scanner.nextInt();\n        \n        int[] sequence = new int[n];\n        int[] prefixParity = new int[n];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            sequence[i] = scanner.nextInt();\n            if (i == 0) {\n                prefixParity[i] = (sequence[i] & 1) == 0 ? 1 : -1;\n            } else {\n                prefixParity[i] = prefixParity[i-1] + ((sequence[i] & 1) == 0 ? 1 : -1);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        PriorityQueue<Transition> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {\n            int diff = Math.abs(sequence[i+1] - sequence[i]);\n            pq.offer(new Transition(diff, i));\n        }\n        \n        int operations = 0;\n        while (!pq.isEmpty()) {\n            Transition t = pq.poll();\n            if (k >= t.cost && prefixParity[t.index] == 0) {\n                k -= t.cost;\n                operations++;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(operations);\n    }\n    \n    static class Transition implements Comparable<Transition> {\n        int cost;\n        int index;\n        \n        Transition(int c, int idx) {\n            cost = c;\n            index = idx;\n        }\n        \n        @Override\n        public int compareTo(Transition other) {\n            if (cost != other.cost) return Integer.compare(cost, other.cost);\n            return Integer.compare(index, other.index);\n        }\n    }\n}\n</your_rewritten_code_5>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    \n    sequence = []\n    prefixParity = []\n    \n    index = 2\n    for i in range(n):\n        val = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n        sequence.append(val)\n        if i == 0:\n            parity = 1 if (val & 1) == 0 else -1\n            prefixParity.append(parity)\n        else:\n            prev_parity = prefixParity[i-1]\n            parity = prev_parity + (1 if (val & 1) == 0 else -1)\n            prefixParity.append(parity)\n    \n    # Use heapq as a priority queue (min-heap)\n    transitions = []\n    for i in range(n-1):\n        diff = abs(sequence[i+1] - sequence[i])\n        heapq.heappush(transitions, (diff, i))\n    \n    operations = 0\n    while transitions:\n        cost, idx = heapq.heappop(transitions)\n        if k >= cost and prefixParity[idx] == 0:\n            k -= cost\n            operations += 1\n    \n    print(operations)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</